# ServerDash Apple Native Design

- Prefer native macOS structure: `NavigationSplitView`, `.listStyle(.sidebar)`, `Table`, `Toolbar`, `Form`, `Inspector`, SF Symbols.
- Use semantic colors and materials from `AppleDesign`; never introduce raw theme RGB values in feature views.
- Same-kind sibling data belongs in one solid panel with hairline dividers. Use separate cards only for independently selectable VPS objects.
- Glass/material is reserved for overlapping chrome: sidebar, toolbar, sheet, popover. Content panels remain solid.
- Hierarchy comes from SF text styles, weight, spacing, and grayscale. Only actions/selection use the system accent; live/error colors carry real state.
- Use named spacing and radius tiers. Avoid one-off shadows, borders, gradients, and sub-11pt text.
- Metrics use `monospacedDigit()` and update without entrance fades or status flicker.
- Prefer system button styles and at least regular control size; prominent actions need generous hit areas.
- Motion must be interruptible, restrained, and disabled or simplified when Reduce Motion is active.
- Every screen needs a clear title, primary action, empty state, error state, keyboard path, and VoiceOver labels.
- Run `Docs/AppleDesignReview.md` before considering a visual change complete.

Source inspiration: naplesblue/apple-design-skill (MIT), adapted for native macOS SwiftUI.
